WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.643
With Paraglide, messages live
in a JSON file per locale,

2
00:00:04.643 --> 00:00:06.546
and you supply every translation.

3
00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:09.767
It compiles each message
to a typed function,

4
00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.798
so a page ships only what it uses.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.213
General Translation keeps copy inline
and generates the translations.

6
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.378
Your team writes copy
inside a T component,

7
00:00:20.378 --> 00:00:21.678
with no message file.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.539
Then npx gt translate writes
every target locale before the

9
00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:27.083
build.

10
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.146
Reviewers edit them
in the Dashboard,

11
00:00:30.146 --> 00:00:33.617
and Locadex opens pull
requests as code changes.

12
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.738
Your team now ships
German with each release.
